chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Second-Layer Applications"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the book's own source at tag third_edition_print1. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-15T19:00:23Z; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.4." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45, chx:P46, chx:P47, chx:P48, chx:P49, chx:P50, chx:P51, chx:P52, chx:P53, chx:P54, chx:P55, chx:P56, chx:P57, chx:P58, chx:P59, chx:P60, chx:P61, chx:P62, chx:P63, chx:P64, chx:P65, chx:P66, chx:P67, chx:P68, chx:P69, chx:P70, chx:P71, chx:P72, chx:P73, chx:P74, chx:P75, chx:P76, chx:P77, chx:P78, chx:P79, chx:P80, chx:P81, chx:P82, chx:P83 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does Chapter 14 of Mastering Bitcoin (3rd edition) say about the second layers built on Bitcoin, its building blocks, colored coins with single-use seals, pay to contract and client-side validation, payment channels, revocable commitments, hash time lock contracts and the Lightning Network with its onion routing, which of its statements can be recomputed or run on Bitcoin Core 31.1, on five lnd nodes and against the published BOLT test vectors, and what has changed in Bitcoin Core, the BOLTs and the history of the Lightning Network since the book went to print?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-15." .
